{"id": "EUVD-2026-86206", "enisaUuid": "ad869d42-08c4-3b51-a412-2bf670d78e79", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: plda: Protect root bus removal with rescan lock\n\nHold the pci_rescan_remove_lock lock while stopping and removing a root bus\nto avoid racing with concurrent rescan or hotplug operations triggered via\nsysfs.  Such races may lead to use-after-free issues or system crashes.\n\n[bhelgaas: commit log]", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T12:43:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/105f212a21cc6bef6855841216dd476022626170", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb78a1d7a2787758a2d8e1182c346d4349f43260", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e4f9745f016c1631d00a4035b06f6e75d449e01"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93818", "GHSA-jj6g-v59v-gmxq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11106720-cfb6-38b9-b0b0-935a5030b148", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3cec8566-f316-3c32-ab69-384499f22a1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c9113968079140cb2f885631db422170f32105 <105f212a21cc6bef6855841216dd476022626170"}, {"id": "440def7d-47c6-3aaf-a9f6-f909efcfba71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "6a2c4002-5ac7-3da7-94ca-6798a285a168", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c9113968079140cb2f885631db422170f32105 <cb78a1d7a2787758a2d8e1182c346d4349f43260"}, {"id": "84811e56-31a9-3a39-ae63-a3dd2eea579c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "aa2fec39-d2cf-3d15-a70f-cd65692da923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c9113968079140cb2f885631db422170f32105 <4e4f9745f016c1631d00a4035b06f6e75d449e01"}, {"id": "c0cf